  "body": "Raises the conditional exponent from PR870's **0.001661956299899884** to **0.001661957774647029**, a gain of **1.474747145e-9**, using the unchanged U8 local word and PR589 bit supplier.\n\nThe new owner map combines Hao Yan's PR858 T16 construction with a literal five-replica map, preserves each component's event order, and applies nine explicit owner edits. All **95,256 whole-helper roles in 189 complete calls** are checked independently. Idle ranks become `{48:6292,3:1,1:3}`; the prefix is **491 < 512** and physical row coefficient **16469 < 20161**. The `8+8+5` auxiliary bank envelope has an independent coordinate-complement audit; every dedicated bank is removed from the final controller. No optimizer runs during verification.\n\nA separate exact bound covers the fixed U8 widths, existing capacities, whole helpers, retained prefix rule `T <= 22`, and the same outer recipe. Two independently structured enumerations cover all 3,729 relevant remainder vectors and show that neither replica count nor owner placement can improve this reported \u03ba grid within that family. Other local words, capacities, split helpers, prefix analyses and outer recipes remain open.\n\nValidation: **complete cold replays passed on macOS/Python 3.11.15 and Linux aarch64/Python 3.14.8**, including fresh PR589/741/799 ancestry and U8 phases, all T21 controller/invoice/admission checks, two exact moment engines and all 47 outer inequalities. Each platform also passed 19 package-boundary rejections, two recompression positives, and the independent packing bound with three controls. Exact mathematical fields and complete owner/plan semantics agree across platforms. Receipts are in `research/complex-t21-owners-validation`; CI reruns the cold chain on Python 3.11 and 3.14.\n\n```sh\npython -B research/complex-t21-owners/verify.py --work /tmp/t21-cold\npython -B research/complex-t21-owners/package_controls.py \\\n  --replay /tmp/t21-cold --baseline799 /tmp/t21-cold/baseline799 \\\n  --ancestor741 /tmp/t21-cold/baseline799/ancestor --out /tmp/t21-controls.json\npython -B research/complex-t21-owner-bound/run.py --out /tmp/t21-bound\n```\n\nCredits and exact source pins for PR858, PR869/870, PR799, PR741 and the earlier controller/bit lineage are retained. All-size compilation, common-label/mutable-source realization, whole-call hosting, precision/tape, analytic transfer and bit H1\u2013H5 remain inherited hypotheses. This is a finite conditional composition, not an unconditional multiplication theorem.\n",
